2. Plans

The right to use the Software is granted per installation (an "instance") under
one of the plans offered by the copyright holder. The plan of an instance is the
license assigned to it through Matmon Cloud, or a license file issued by the
copyright holder for an installation that does not connect to Matmon Cloud.

a) Personal (free of charge). You may install and use the Software free of
   charge for PERSONAL, NON-COMMERCIAL purposes only: to monitor your own home
   network and devices you use privately. Personal does not cover use by or on
   behalf of a business, a public body or any other organization, use in
   connection with a trade, business or profession, or use to monitor devices
   or networks of others, whether paid or not. The limits of the Personal plan
   (for example one probe) are enforced by the Software.

b) Business and Enterprise (paid). Any use not covered by Personal requires a
   paid plan for each instance on which the Software is used that way. The
   scope, limits and price of a plan are those stated when the plan is
   acquired.

c) Partners. A service partner of the copyright holder may provide plans to its
   customers under its own agreement with them. The partner's customers use the
   Software within the plan the partner assigned.

d) Cloud packages. Cloud packages add services of Matmon Cloud (for example
   cloud sensors, text messages and phone calls) to an organization. They do not
   grant the right to use the Software on an instance.

